  "security_implications": "keys_en directly controls sideload key output; its unconditional assertion in Idle combined with the combinational path creates a risk that keys_en is high during a wipe request (U1). The terminal state StSideloadStop permanently disables sideload after wipe, which is a security posture but lacks documented recovery (U2). Error handling on invalid state (U3) freezes the FSM and may bypass key zeroization or leave the system in an unprotected state. The fsm_err_o signal presumably feeds a system-wide security alert, but its exact routing is unknown here (U4).",
